    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Standard (i.e., two-marker) interval mapping can be extended to multipoint interval mapping by considering all linked markers on a chromosome (Fulker et al. 1995, Kruglyak and Lander 1995b). In the approach of Fulker et al., the two-marker regression estimate of the QTL ibd status (Equation 16.43) is replaced by a multiple regression that incorporates all n linked markers on a chromosome,",
